      "text": "We start by completing the square to transform the given equation into a perfect square form. The given equation is:\n\n\\[\nx^2 + 1992x = 1993\n\\]\n\nTo complete the square, we add and subtract the square of half the coefficient of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx^2 + 1992x + 996^2 - 996^2 = 1993\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(x + 996)^2 - 996^2 = 1993\n\\]\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square term by adding \\(996^2\\) to both sides:\n\n\\[\n(x + 996)^2 = 1993 + 996^2\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(996^2\\):\n\n\\[\n996^2 = (1000 - 4)^2 = 1000^2 - 2 \\cdot 1000 \\cdot 4 + 4^2 = 1000000 - 8000 + 16 = 992016\n\\]\n\nNow add 1993 to 992016:\n\n\\[\n1993 + 992016 = 994009\n\\]\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n(x + 996)^2 = 994009\n\\]\n\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\nx + 996 = \\pm \\sqrt{994009}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(994009 = 999^2\\), we have:\n\n\\[\nx + 996 = \\pm 999\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\n\\[\nx + 996 = 999 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x + 996 = -999\n\\]\n\nSolving these equations, we get:\n\n\\[\nx = 999 - 996 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = -999 - 996 = -1995\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the solutions is:\n\n\\[\n3 + (-1995) = 3 - 1995 = -1992\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of the values of \\(x\\) which satisfy the equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1992}\n\\]",
